{:event/actor "seb" :event/at #inst "2026-08-05T22:20:37.902Z" :event/body {:fact/path [:summary] :fact/value "tik.args/parse-value reads a bare word as EDN and falls back to a keyword, so a uuid beginning a-f parses as a keyword (:fadff5da-...) while one beginning 0-9 parses as a string. Two ticket ids, two types, from the same code path — and any fact whose value happens to be a uuid inherits the split. Surfaced by probe_test/reserved_names_cannot_be_shadowed_by_a_fact, which asserted the string form and therefore failed on roughly 37% of runs (6 of 16 leading hex digits are letters); the test now matches either form, so the gate is honest, but the parse behaviour is untouched. Deciding it means choosing what a uuid-shaped bare word IS — a string, a keyword, or #uuid — and the answer affects values already stored in every store, so it wants a verdict rather than a patch."} :event/parents #{"sha256-87bb9688621a5c0b54c180673b253bb72c88b1897a01c303636aa4bcde6dc74c"} :event/ticket #uuid "15d905a7-4536-40ed-9562-c423ca28dc1e" :event/type :fact/assert}